.\" Man page for the Ferngeist gateway environment variables.
.\" Keep in sync with internal/config/config.go and docs/configuration.md.
.TH FERNGEIST-GATEWAY-ENV 1 "2026-10-20" "ferngeist-gateway" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferngeist\-gateway\-env \- environment variables for the Ferngeist gateway
.SH SYNOPSIS
Environment variables read by
.BR ferngeist\-gateway (1).
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Ferngeist Gateway
is configured through environment variables and persisted state. This page
documents every variable the daemon reads.
.PP
Explicit environment variables take precedence over persisted settings. The
persisted settings are the gateway name, public base URL, LAN flag, and
registry URL; they fill in a value only when the corresponding variable is not
set.
.SS Value parsing
.TP
.B Booleans
Unless noted otherwise, a boolean is enabled by
.IR 1 ,
.IR true ,
or
.I yes
(case\-insensitive) and disabled by any other value.
.TP
.B Integers
A positive integer. An unset, unparsable, zero, or negative value falls back
to the default.
.TP
.B Durations
A positive integer number of seconds. An unset, unparsable, zero, or negative
value falls back to the default, except for
.BR FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_CREDENTIAL_GRACE_SECONDS ,
where
.I 0
is meaningful and disables the grace window.
.TP
.B Paths
Relative paths resolve from the daemon's working directory. For a service
install, that is the install's data directory.
.SH "NETWORK AND IDENTITY"
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LISTEN_ADDR
Public API listen address.
Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1:5788 .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_ADMIN_ADDR
Local admin API listen address. The admin API should stay bound to localhost.
Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1:5789 .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_ENABLE_LAN
Enable LAN discovery and access. Enabled only when set to
.IR 1 .
Default: disabled.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_NAME
Gateway name advertised to clients. Default: the hostname, or
.I ferngeist\-gateway
when the hostname cannot be read.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL
Public URL clients use to reach the gateway. Setting it puts the gateway in
public mode, which turns on the strict security defaults below. Default:
unset.
.SH "STORAGE AND LOGGING"
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_STATE_DB
SQLite state database path. Default:
.I ferngeist\-gateway.db
in the daemon's working directory.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_DIR
Log directory. Default:
.I logs
in the daemon's working directory.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_LEVEL
Log level:
.IR debug ,
.IR info ,
.IR warn ,
or
.IR error .
Default:
.IR info .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_MAX_BYTES
Maximum size of a log file before rotation, in bytes. Default: 1048576
(1 MiB).
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_MAX_BACKUPS
Number of rotated log files to keep. Default: 3.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_FRAME_LOG
Append every client\-to\-agent and agent\-to\-client ACP JSON\-RPC frame to
.IR <log dir>/<agent>\-agent.log
as newline\-delimited JSON, rotated with
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_MAX_BYTES
and
.BR FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_MAX_BACKUPS .
This is a debugging aid: frames can contain project code, tool output, and
secrets. Default: disabled.
.SH AGENTS
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_REGISTRY_URL
ACP registry URL. Default: the ACP registry at
.IR https://cdn.agentclientprotocol.com/registry/v1/latest/registry.json .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_MANAGED_BIN_DIR
Directory for installed agent binaries and npm agent installs. Default is
platform\-dependent:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Linux:
.IR ~/.local/share/ferngeist\-gateway/bin
.IP \(bu 2
macOS:
.IR "~/Library/Application Support/Ferngeist Gateway/bin"
.IP \(bu 2
Windows:
.IR "%LocalAppData%\(rsFerngeistGateway\(rsbin"
.RE
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_JS_RUNTIME
Runtime used to launch npm\-distributed registry agents:
.IR auto
(bun when it is on
.IR PATH ,
else node),
.IR bun ,
.IR node ,
or
.IR npm
(launch through
.IR "npm exec" ).
Default:
.IR auto .
.SH "REMOTE ACCESS"
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_TAILSCALE_MODE
Automatic remote\-access provisioning:
.IR off ,
.IR auto
(the Tailscale CLI when available, otherwise the embedded node),
.IR cli ,
or
.IR tsnet .
Any mode other than
.I off
is treated as intended public exposure, so the strict security defaults apply
from the first boot. Default:
.IR off .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_TAILSCALE_AUTH_KEY
Pre\-authentication key for the embedded Tailscale node. Setting it skips the
interactive login. Default: unset.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_TAILSCALE_HOSTNAME
Tailnet device name for the embedded node. Default:
.IR ferngeist\-gateway .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_TAILSCALE_PRIVATE
Use
.I serve
or
.I ListenTLS
so the gateway is reachable only from the tailnet, instead of public Funnel.
Default: disabled.
.SH "PAIRING AND CREDENTIALS"
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_REQUIRE_PROOF_OF_POSSESSION
Require proof\-of\-possession for authenticated requests. Default: enabled in
public mode (a public base URL or any Tailscale mode other than
.IR off ),
disabled otherwise. An explicit value always wins.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_ALLOW_LEGACY_BEARER_CREDENTIALS
Allow bearer\-only credentials. Default: disabled in public mode, enabled
otherwise. An explicit value always wins.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_CREDENTIAL_TTL_SECONDS
Lifetime of a paired device token. Default: 604800 (7 days).
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_CREDENTIAL_GRACE_SECONDS
How long an expired credential stays recoverable through the client's
credential refresh call. Set to
.I 0
to disable the grace window and hard\-delete on expiry. Default: 7776000
(90 days).
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PAIRING_ARM_TTL_SECONDS
How long a locally approved pairing stays valid. Default: 120 (2 minutes).
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PAIRING_MAX_ATTEMPTS
Maximum failed pairing attempts before lockout. Default: 5.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PAIRING_LOCKOUT_SECONDS
Lockout duration after too many failed attempts. Default: 120 (2 minutes).
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PAIRING_START_REFILL_SECONDS
Rate\-limit refill interval for pairing start. Default: 5.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PAIRING_COMPLETE_REFILL_SECONDS
Rate\-limit refill interval for pairing complete. Default: 2.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PAIRING_BURST_PER_IP
Per\-IP burst limit for pairing requests. Default: 5.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PAIRING_BURST_GLOBAL
Global burst limit for pairing requests. Default: 30.
.SH SESSIONS
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_SESSION_MAX_DISCONNECTED_SECONDS
How long a disconnected session is kept before the reaper closes it.
Default: 900 (15 minutes).
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_MAX_SESSIONS_PER_DEVICE
Maximum concurrent sessions a single device may hold. Default: 5.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PROGRESS_INTERVAL_SECONDS
Minimum time between live progress pushes while an agent is mid\-turn.
Default: 15.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_ALLOW_REMOTE_DIAGNOSTICS_EXPORT
Allow the remote diagnostics export endpoint. Default: disabled.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_ALLOW_REMOTE_RUNTIME_RESTART_ENV
Allow restarting a runtime with a client\-supplied environment. Default:
disabled.
.SH UPDATES
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_UPDATE_CHECK_ENABLED
Check GitHub Releases for a newer stable version at startup and on an
interval, and push an update\-available notification to paired devices. Only
.I 0
or
.I false
disables it. Default: enabled. Package\-manager builds are expected to disable
it in their service environment.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_UPDATE_CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS
Seconds between update checks. Default: 86400 (24 hours).
.SH NOTES
Environment variables are read at daemon startup. Changing one requires
restarting the daemon, for example with
.BR "ferngeist\-gateway daemon restart" .
.PP
For a Linux service install, put custom variables in
.I config/daemon.override.env
next to
.IR config/daemon.env :
the unit loads the override file last, and it is never rewritten by
.BR "daemon install" .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ferngeist\-gateway (1),
.IR docs/configuration.md ,
.IR docs/security.md .
.PP
.IR https://github.com/arafatamim/ferngeist\-acp\-gateway .
